From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tanjilbhuiyan <tanjilbhuiyan@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 15:06:01 +0600
Subject: [PATCH 70/70] net: wireless: samsung: scsc: always create
 /sys/wifi/mac_addr

The MAC-override sysfs file was only created when Samsung's SEP (One UI)
version macro is >= 9, which only the vendor build defines, so it never
existed on 6.18 (M9.4 M9E: the ADR-0009 runtime hook found no
/sys/wifi/mac_addr and the driver fell back to a random address). Create
and remove it unconditionally; it is the driver's address-override
interface.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: I13a2a841cb289c89799ca01629b97badaddb0cfe
---
 drivers/net/wireless/samsung/scsc/dev.c | 9 ++++-----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/samsung/scsc/dev.c b/drivers/net/wireless/samsung/scsc/dev.c
index 7f6482f52..ab0bac334 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/samsung/scsc/dev.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/samsung/scsc/dev.c
@@ -665,10 +665,11 @@ int __init slsi_dev_load(void)
 	sap_dbg_init();
 	sap_test_init();
 
-/* Always create devnode if TW Android P on */
-#if defined(SCSC_SEP_VERSION) && SCSC_SEP_VERSION >= 9
+/*
+ * 6.18 port: always create /sys/wifi/mac_addr. 4.14 tied it to Samsung's SEP (One UI) version macro, which only
+ * the vendor build defines; the 6.18 runtime passes the factory MAC through it (ADR-0009).
+ */
 	slsi_create_sysfs_macaddr();
-#endif
 	SLSI_INFO_NODEV("--- Maxwell Wi-Fi driver loaded successfully ---\n");
 	return 0;
 }
@@ -677,9 +678,7 @@ void __exit slsi_dev_unload(void)
 {
 	SLSI_INFO_NODEV("Unloading Maxwell Wi-Fi driver\n");
 
-#if defined(SCSC_SEP_VERSION) && SCSC_SEP_VERSION >= 9
 	slsi_destroy_sysfs_macaddr();
-#endif
 	/* Unregister SAPs */
 	sap_mlme_deinit();
 	sap_ma_deinit();
